      "message": "Considering the heat stack are going to be stored in untrusted-projects, it might be good to document the security implication of applying a malicious template. I presume the created resources are well scoped and isolated inside the openstack tenant, but I can\u0027t tell if Heat is designed and equiped to handle such untrusted templates to be applied inside a single tenant.\n\nFor example https://docs.openstack.org/heat/latest/template_guide/openstack.html#OS::Nova::KeyPair-props-opt has a \"save_private_key\", couldn\u0027t that be used to mutate an existing key?",
